sequenceDiagram
    participant Docs as Private Docs<br/>(your disk)
    participant srv as MCP Server<br/>(your machine)
    participant CDB as ChromaDB<br/>(your disk)
    participant CD as Claude Desktop<br/>(your machine)
    participant Ant as Anthropic API<br/>(cloud)

    Note over Docs,CDB: INDEXING — stays 100% local, no network
    Docs->>srv: Raw markdown text (read from disk)
    srv->>CDB: Embeddings + metadata (written to disk)
    Note over CDB: ~/.mcp-kb/chroma/ — never leaves machine

    Note over srv,Ant: QUERY — only retrieved snippet crosses network
    CD->>srv: search_docs("how to rollback?") — via stdio (local IPC)
    srv->>CDB: ANN search (local disk read)
    CDB-->>srv: 5 matching chunks (~2,000 tokens total)
    srv-->>CD: Chunks with citations — still local
    CD->>Ant: Full conversation context including retrieved chunks
    Ant-->>CD: Claude's response

    Note over Docs,Ant: Your 1.1M other passages? Never touched.<br/>Only the retrieved snippet enters the conversation.
